  "limitations": [
    "The side photograph establishes the double upsweep and ribbed covering of the shelter. The tour shows reed courses changing direction across the framed panels under the gable. Exact roof dimensions and materials, rear wall depths and concealed construction remain estimated.",
    "The separate roadside arch, clay relief wall and two iron leaves follow the 2019 exterior photo and 2022 virtual tour. The shape behind the visible sculpted surfaces remains estimated.",
    "Panorama-constrained placement on the western grove approach. The sheltered portal faces west-southwest, and the ironwork follows the mapped road. The rebuilt apron and local grades join the thresholds and underlying terrain. Dimensions, exact verge elevations and the trail beyond the portal remain approximate.",
    "Distinct motifs on the iron leaves follow the photographed bent drummer and his drum, stretched fish-tailed figure, broad bowl and seated bearer, draped standing musicians and large incised vessel. Fine facial relief and tool marks remain interpreted."
  ],
